# Go generated files

# Compiled binaries and plugins
# NOTE: `go build` on a main package emits an extension-less binary that no
# pattern here can match. Exercism Go exercises are library packages (see
# go.mod: `module lasagna`, not main), so this doesn't come up. If you ever
# `go build -o foo`, add `foo` below.
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib
*.a
*.o

# Test binaries, debugger, coverage output
*.test
*.out
__debug_bin*
coverage.txt
coverage.html

# go.sum is deliberately NOT ignored: it is a cryptographic checksum file, not a
# resolution cache. Committing it is Go's official guidance, and without it
# `go test` hard-fails on any exercise that has a dependency.

# Workspace / tooling
go.work
go.work.sum
vendor/
bin/
.idea/
